 "evidence": "Single-particle physics with published laws fitted on Earth (mass, area, fall law, capacitance, ventilation, sticking), carried to lunar gravity and air through the quantities they depend on; idealised columns and clouds. A first estimate of the sky winter's snow, not a cloud model.",
 "reading_rule": "Sizes are maximum dimensions. vapour_growth starts a 0.2 mm crystal at each cloud top and grows it from the vapour alone to the freezing level, with the cloud's depth and the air's mass in it, which at one mixing ratio of cloud ice sets the ice a falling flake can sweep up; crossing_hours are the hours a flake of a set size takes from the cloud top to the freezing level; melting gives, for flakes of set sizes falling from the freezing level through air at a set relative humidity, the depths below it where half and all of the ice has melted. The Moon's column is the resort's sky ladder at 301 K; Earth's a winter column with its freezing level at 850 hPa."
}
